WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.450
In 2024 to 25, Belfast City Council
collected 161,320 tonnes of waste.

2
00:00:09.500 --> 00:00:13.250
Household waste came to
397 kilograms per person,

3
00:00:13.300 --> 00:00:16.430
the lowest of Northern
Ireland's 11 councils.

4
00:00:16.480 --> 00:00:21.170
Just 0.9 per cent of what Belfast
collected went to landfill.

5
00:00:21.220 --> 00:00:24.930
Across Northern Ireland, the
figure was 14.0 per cent.

6
00:00:24.980 --> 00:00:29.090
So why might Belfast run
short of room for new homes?

7
00:00:29.140 --> 00:00:32.390
In this mission, you'll work
down the waste hierarchy,

8
00:00:32.440 --> 00:00:36.770
from reduce to landfill, and
grade Belfast at every step.

9
00:00:36.820 --> 00:00:40.830
Then you'll compare how Belfast's homes
are heated with how homes are heated across

10
00:00:40.880 --> 00:00:42.290
Northern Ireland.

11
00:00:42.340 --> 00:00:46.530
Your mission: judge how sustainably
Belfast uses its resources,

12
00:00:46.580 --> 00:00:48.350
and what could limit its growth.
